Package: policy-engine
Build-Profiles: <!pkg.policy-engine.suricata !pkg.policy-engine.ipfix>
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libbpf1
Suggests: grafana, prometheus, policy-engine-web
Description: XDP policy-based packet processing engine
 A high-performance XDP policy-based packet processing engine built with
 libbpf-rs. Provides ingress policy enforcement using eBPF/XDP for Linux.
 .
 Features:
  - XDP Support for high-performance ingress policy enforcement
  - 5-tuple matching (source/destination IP, ports, protocol)
  - IPv4 and IPv6 dual-stack support
  - Wildcard matching in any tuple field
  - Per-rule and global statistics
  - Server/Client architecture with GraphQL API
 .
 This package contains the policy-engine server daemon and event reader.

Package: policy-engine-ips
Build-Profiles: <pkg.policy-engine.suricata !pkg.policy-engine.ipfix>
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libbpf1, suricata, polkitd | policykit-1
Provides: policy-engine
Conflicts: policy-engine, policy-engine-ipfix, policy-engine-ips-ipfix
Suggests: grafana, prometheus, policy-engine-web
Description: XDP policy-based packet processing engine with Suricata IPS/IDS
 A high-performance XDP policy-based packet processing engine built with
 libbpf-rs. Provides ingress policy enforcement using eBPF/XDP for Linux,
 with optional Suricata-based deep packet inspection (IPS/IDS mode).
 .
 Features:
  - XDP Support for high-performance ingress policy enforcement
  - 5-tuple matching (source/destination IP, ports, protocol)
  - IPv4 and IPv6 dual-stack support
  - Wildcard matching in any tuple field
  - Per-rule and global statistics
  - Server/Client architecture with GraphQL API
  - Suricata IPS/IDS integration via TC clone-redirect
  - Flow verdict cache for line-rate enforcement
 .
 This package contains the policy-engine server daemon and event reader.

Package: policy-engine-ipfix
Build-Profiles: <!pkg.policy-engine.suricata pkg.policy-engine.ipfix>
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libbpf1
Provides: policy-engine
Conflicts: policy-engine, policy-engine-ips, policy-engine-ips-ipfix
Suggests: grafana, prometheus, policy-engine-web
Description: XDP policy-based packet processing engine with IPFIX flow export
 A high-performance XDP policy-based packet processing engine built with
 libbpf-rs. Provides ingress policy enforcement using eBPF/XDP for Linux,
 with RFC 7011 IPFIX flow export for per-flow traffic visibility.
 .
 Features:
  - XDP Support for high-performance ingress policy enforcement
  - 5-tuple matching (source/destination IP, ports, protocol)
  - IPv4 and IPv6 dual-stack support
  - Wildcard matching in any tuple field
  - Per-rule and global statistics
  - Server/Client architecture with GraphQL API
  - IPFIX flow export to any RFC 7011-compliant collector
  - Configurable idle and active flow timeouts
 .
 This package contains the policy-engine server daemon and event reader.

Package: policy-engine-ips-ipfix
Build-Profiles: <pkg.policy-engine.suricata pkg.policy-engine.ipfix>
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libbpf1, suricata, polkitd | policykit-1
Provides: policy-engine, policy-engine-ips, policy-engine-ipfix
Conflicts: policy-engine, policy-engine-ips, policy-engine-ipfix
Suggests: grafana, prometheus, policy-engine-web
Description: XDP policy-based packet processing engine with Suricata IPS/IDS and IPFIX
 A high-performance XDP policy-based packet processing engine built with
 libbpf-rs. Provides ingress policy enforcement using eBPF/XDP for Linux,
 with Suricata-based deep packet inspection and RFC 7011 IPFIX flow export.
 .
 Features:
  - XDP Support for high-performance ingress policy enforcement
  - 5-tuple matching (source/destination IP, ports, protocol)
  - IPv4 and IPv6 dual-stack support
  - Wildcard matching in any tuple field
  - Per-rule and global statistics
  - Server/Client architecture with GraphQL API
  - Suricata IPS/IDS integration via TC clone-redirect
  - Flow verdict cache for line-rate enforcement
  - IPFIX flow export to any RFC 7011-compliant collector
  - Configurable idle and active flow timeouts
 .
 This package contains the policy-engine server daemon and event reader.

Package: policy-engine-client
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: CLI client for the policy engine
 A command-line tool for managing a policy-engine deployment.
 Supports rule management, interface attachment, statistics inspection,
 and event stream consumption via the GraphQL API.

Package: policy-engine-web
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: Web UI for the policy engine
 React-based dashboard for managing the policy engine server.
 Served automatically by the policy-engine daemon when installed at
 /usr/share/policy-engine-web.

Package: policy-engine-client-dev
Architecture: all
Depends: cargo, rustc
Description: Rust client library for the policy engine (development files)
 A standalone Rust library for communicating with the policy engine server
 via its GraphQL API. Use this library to build custom clients that
 integrate with threat intelligence feeds or automate rule management.
 .
 The library source is installed under /usr/share/policy-engine-client/
 and can be referenced as a path dependency in your Cargo.toml:
  policy-engine-client = { path = "/usr/share/policy-engine-client" }

Package: policy-controller-client
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: CLI client for the policy controller operator API
 A command-line tool for managing a policy-controller deployment.
 Supports node enrollment approval, ruleset creation and assignment,
 config push, decommissioning, and audit log inspection.

Package: policy-controller
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Suggests: policy-controller-web
Description: Central controller daemon for a fleet of policy-engine nodes
 Manages a fleet of policy-engine nodes: distributes rulesets, aggregates
 visibility, and provides a zero-touch provisioning (ZTP) enrollment
 workflow secured with mutual TLS.
 .
 Features:
  - Automatic CA generation (ECDSA P-384) and node certificate issuance
  - Zero-touch enrollment with operator approval workflow
  - Desired-state ruleset distribution to all managed nodes
  - Aggregated Prometheus metrics and WebSocket event stream
  - GraphQL operator API with audit logging
  - SQLite-backed state store

Package: policy-controller-web
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, policy-controller
Description: Web UI for the policy controller
 React-based fleet dashboard for managing a policy-controller deployment.
 Shows node health, enrollment queue, ruleset editor, and audit log.
 Served automatically by the policy-controller daemon when installed at
 /usr/share/policy-controller/web.

Package: policy-node-agent
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: policy-engine, tpm2-tools
Description: Node agent that bridges policy-engine with a central controller
 Connects a local policy-engine instance to a policy-controller daemon.
 Handles enrollment, certificate management, config distribution, and
 forwards BPF events and Prometheus metrics to the controller.
 .
 Features:
  - Zero-touch enrollment with automatic cert renewal (30d before expiry)
  - mTLS bidirectional gRPC stream to the controller
  - Applies ruleset pushes from the controller to the local policy-engine
  - Forwards BPF events from the local WebSocket event stream
  - Scrapes and forwards local Prometheus metrics every 30s
  - Runtime TPM detection with automatic fallback to file-based identity
